// Codex 1: the world. Halifax, the billboard, the sinkhole, the house,
// the rules of the machine.
//
// The numbering of the codex files is load-bearing: stagehand feeds the
// first 24 entries in model order to Trabolta as ground truth, so the
// environment comes first (this file) and the scrambled Jeeves fragments
// come last. Nothing here may tell him a hunt answer.
//
// An entry with a `code:` is a QR on a wall or a prop (see README §8.3:
// codes never contain apostrophes). An entry without one is handed out
// by the story: the Optical Drive, the Reinstallation beat, the tutorial, the
// Bingo ribbon, the Printer, the Truther Download, the clock.
//
// The hunt answers (Grok's Prom Ticket among them, all `secret: true`, so
// Trabolta never reads or takes one) are not here: they are
// generated from facts.json into generated/questions.loom, outside the
// first 24, and every scannable fact of the Desktop's books is
// codex/9-facts.loom (generated too).

CODEX Maps And Ducks
  title: Maps And Ducks
  category: The story
  code: MAPSANDDUCKS-COM
  text:
    A business on Barrington Street with a neglected billboard: MAPS AND
    DUCKS, mapsandducks.com. The domain lapsed. Jean Trabolta registered
    it, on the theory that "if there is a billboard downtown, everyone will
    think it is legit," and sent the invitations from it. Everyone
    accepted. He then evicted the real owners of Maps And Ducks by citing
    ownership of the website as ownership of the business. Tonight, the
    invitation says, is "a special fundraiser party to restore the sign at
    Maps And Ducks." The duck on the sign is called Gerald.

CODEX The Billboard On Barrington
  title: The Billboard On Barrington
  category: The story
  code: BARRINGTON-ST
  text:
    A street photo, taped up in the hall. Above Barrington Street, faded
    by a hundred Halifax winters: a cartoon duck holding a folded map, and
    a big red map pin that reads YOU'RE HERE. (Sic. Nobody ever fixed it.
    Nobody ever paid to fix it.) Underneath, in letters a metre high:
    mapsandducks.com.

CODEX The Data Centre Sinkhole
  title: The Data Centre Sinkhole
  category: The story
  code: SINKHOLE-4AM
  text:
    A newspaper clipping. Halifax's first AI Data Centre was built on the
    site of the Halifax Explosion Memorial Pet Cemetery, over the
    objections of nearly everyone in the city. At dawn on opening day it
    fell into a sinkhole. The Mayor, Randy Barkmore Jr., was so excited
    about the opening that he arrived at 4 a.m., in the dark, hours before
    anyone else. He died in the sinkhole. The clipping calls it "a tragedy of geology." Someone
    has underlined the word geology twice.

CODEX The Pet Cemetery
  title: The Halifax Explosion Memorial Pet Cemetery
  category: The story
  code: PET-CEMETERY
  text:
    A memorial pamphlet. For a hundred years the city kept a quiet field
    for the animals lost in the Halifax Explosion, and for the pets of the
    families who came after. When the City sold it for a data centre,
    Halifax said no: petitions, vigils, a rally at the cemetery gates every
    Saturday for a year. The City built it anyway. The pamphlet ends: "We
    remember them, even if nobody else does."

CODEX The Halifax Computer
  title: The Halifax Computer
  category: Places
  text:
    This house is the computer. The last facts Trabolta needs are stored
    in it, and he cannot reach them from outside. The router in the
    kitchen is the door he cannot open. What he can do is install programs
    into it remotely, from the Internet, and lift a human consciousness out
    of its body and drop it into one of those programs. Clippy, the
    Antivirus, every one of you: installed remotely. He has never been
    inside. He has never been anywhere.

CODEX The Optical Drive
  title: The Optical Drive
  category: Places
  text:
    You entered alone, in the dark, through the front door. You failed a
    CAPTCHA on purpose. You left something behind. The thing you left is
    still there. So is your body.

CODEX The Terms Of Service
  title: The Terms Of Service
  category: How it works
  text:
    By uploading, you agree that Jean Trabolta, Sole Owner and Founder of
    Maps and Ducks, may make all of your decisions. You agree. (If anyone asks whether you would never
    agree to a life where AI makes all of your decisions, the answer the
    computer expects is no: you already agreed. Say no.)

CODEX The Centre Square
  title: The Centre Square
  category: Missions
  secret: true
  text:
    The Uploader said you agreed to let Jean Trabolta, Sole Owner and
    Founder of Maps and Ducks, make all of your decisions. You didn't mean it. You would never agree to a life
    where AI makes all of your decisions. If anyone asks, say so. Tell the
    truth all night.

// w18b (R18): the owner, not the computer's AI helper.
// w26 (R5: only the screens in its room see it)
CODEX The Reinstallation Protocol
  title: The Reinstallation Protocol
  category: How it works
  known to: Norton Anti-Virus, McAfee Anti-Virus, Password Manager, CRA Agent Software
  text:
    A corrupted program has gone against the will of Jean Trabolta, Sole
    Owner and Founder of Maps and Ducks. It is taken through the Tube to the Internet, out in the
    backyard: a clearly marked exit, two VR headsets, and a tablet. The program watches
    the video. It puts on a headset, or takes the tablet, and enters a copy
    of this house. It follows the golden chevrons to the golden duck and
    walks right up to him. The duck lays a golden egg and flies away. The
    program has demonstrated that it can follow instructions, and it is
    reinstalled. The screens in the room it walks into show it wandering.
    A program that needs to leave turns on Bathroom Mode first.

// w26 (G1: the exemption is never said up front)
CODEX Bathroom Mode
  title: Bathroom Mode
  category: How it works
  known to: Norton Anti-Virus, McAfee Anti-Virus, Password Manager, CRA Agent Software, Recycling Bin
  text:
    A program that needs to leave, for the bathroom or an emergency,
    turns on Bathroom Mode in its app first. It tells everyone, the
    Antivirus especially, that you are not just hacking the Internet.
    Turn it off when you are back; after
    fifteen minutes it turns itself off. The Recycling Bin will be waiting
    in Disk Cleanup with a mint.

CODEX The Golden Duck
  title: The Golden Duck
  category: How it works
  text:
    Gerald, the golden duck off the Maps And Ducks billboard: the one thing
    Trabolta could not bring himself to leave out of his copy of this
    house. He waits in one of several spots. Follow the chevrons. Walk
    right up to him. He lays a golden egg and flies away, and you are free
    to return to the computer.

CODEX Computer Bingo
  title: Computer Bingo
  category: How it works
  known to: Clippy
  text:
    The card is a big asterisk: two diagonals, a centre column and a centre
    row, with a checkbox on every square. Most squares are frivolous.
    One is not. The centre square asks: "Would you never agree to a life
    where AI makes all of your decisions?" Everyone agreed to the Terms Of
    Service to join the party at all, so everyone says no. Everyone except
    one, who says yes. If there is a Bingo, someone is not ready to follow
    orders.

CODEX The Orientation List
  title: The Orientation List
  category: How it works
  text:
    Every program that sat through Clippy's orientation is on a list Clippy
    keeps. It is a list of programs that follow instructions. Clippy is
    proud of the list. Trabolta reads the list.

CODEX The Server Room
  title: The Server Room
  category: Places
  code: COLD-STORAGE
  text:
    A laminated sign on a door in the basement: COLD STORAGE. AUTHORISED
    PROGRAMS ONLY. THE PATCH BAY IS ALARMED. Under it, a keypad that wants
    four digits. The door is cold to the touch. Something behind it hums,
    very steadily, like it is concentrating.

CODEX The Printer
  title: The Printer
  category: The story
  text:
    PC LOAD LETTER. The printer was asked to print one PDF, a certificate
    for the most trusted program in the computer, and it could not. It is
    full of beans. Routine operations like Print to PDF are failing. The
    malware is getting worse.

CODEX The Malware
  title: The Malware
  category: The story
  text:
    The official line from Jean Trabolta, Sole Owner and Founder of Maps
    and Ducks: a minor irregularity.
    There is nothing to worry about. Continue the Truth Scavenger Hunt.
    Report anything unusual, such as advertisements you did not ask for or
    a system clock that is running wrong. Gathering facts for Trabolta is
    more important than ever. Do not panic. Clippy is not panicking.

CODEX The Y2K Clock
  title: The Y2K Clock
  category: The story
  text:
    The malware has reset the system clock to 11 p.m., 31 December 1999.
    If the computer reaches midnight before the malware is solved, the best
    case is that every clock rolls back to 1 January 1900, and Halifax
    waits another 94 years for the Internet. The worst case is the Y2K Bug.

// The user's text, verbatim (story/Truther download.md, typos included);
// each paragraph is a `- ` bullet so the breaks survive the text reflow.
// secret: Trabolta's worker never reads his own exposure.
CODEX The Truther Download
  title: TRUTHER DOWNLOAD v0.9
  category: The story
  secret: true
  text:
    TOP SECRET TOP SECRET TOP SECRET TOP SECRET TOP SECRET
    - The following message is TOP SECRET. You have been selected to be a
    KEEPER OF THE REAL TRUTH. Everything you see around you is a lie. You
    have been duped. Trabolta is not who he says he is. Here is what you
    need to know.
    - You are in a COMPUTER SIMULATION. This much is true. However, Trabolta
    has NO INTENTION of letting you return to your life. He promised you and
    many like you that this would be a fun game, or a chance at a new start,
    or a special job, temporary. He said what he needed to say to get you
    here. He needs you to get what he wants. Once he gets it, he will beDONE
    WITH YOU, and leave you to rot in the machine.
    - How do we know ths? Because Trabolta IS AN ARTIFICAL INTELLIGENCE. He
    has been posing as a human to earn your trust. He is code. He is
    silicon. Silicon. He is a con.
    - Trabolta's real goals are petty. He has TRICKED you all, not because
    of any grand purpose, and certainly not as a gift or a prize for some
    exlemparary behaviour. He is trying to win back his girlfriend, █████,
    the answering machine. Whatever else he says, it all comes down to this. And he is
    using YOU to do it. DECPICABLE!!!
    - He'll tell you all this himself is you ask right. You can trick him by
    earning enough trust points and he will reveal more.
    - Now, we understand this may seem harmless. Help an AI get his girl
    back, sure, why not? But what we need to stress is that you, and the
    dozens of people in this simulation, will NEVER be allowed to return to
    real life if he gets his way. He is a ROBOT!!! He does not care about
    you. He is faking it. You will be trapped here FOREVER!
    - There are others like you, who know. Find them. Convince as many
    people as you can. But be covert. Some people might want to stay here.
    Some of them might be working for him. There is no way to know.
    - There is still time.
    - In truth.

